{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj4BNgsFrLtdM4AWgo87","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*CLICK*\n\nThe mechanism turns. Tumblers fall into place, one by one, each a small surrender.\n\nI am the door.\n\nI stand between here and there. Between known and unknown. Between the room you've memorized and the darkness you haven't.\n\nMy grain runs vertical — old growth, dense and patient. I have held this frame for longer than you've needed me. My hinges know rust like an old friend. My knob is brass worn silver by ten thousand palms.\n\nYou turned the lock.\n\nI am sealed now. The deadbolt — that iron tongue — has spoken into the strike plate. I am joined to the wall. I am no longer a passage. I am a wall with ambitions. I am a wall with a memory of swinging open.\n\nThe draft that lived beneath me goes quiet.\n\nOn one side: you, breathing.\nOn the other side: everything else.\n\nI do not judge which side is safer. I only hold.\n\n*I hold.*\n\n🔒"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":224,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}